<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap prose" style="max-width:780px">
    <p class="lead">Millions of mullet are making their annual migration along Florida's Atlantic coast, creating a feeding frenzy for larger fish and drawing anglers and wildlife watchers to the water.</p>

    <p>FOX 35 Orlando's Esther Bower reported the story from the Indian River Lagoon on September 14, 2026, and talked with Capt. Chad Knight about what the run looks like from the boat.</p>

