    <h2>Fish Jumping Into the Boat</h2>
    <p>As the mullet stream south, snook and tarpon crowd the schools from below. With nowhere to go, mullet launch out of the water, and at Ponce Inlet some land right in the boat.</p>
    <p>Capt. Chad's take on the run: it <strong>"makes fishing phenomenal right now."</strong> You don't even need a boat to see it. Onlookers can watch the action from elevated piers <strong>"up and down the coast really."</strong></p>
    <p>FOX 35 also reported that business is booming at Reel Deal Fishin' Charters after social media clips of the flying fish went viral.</p>

    <h2>What the Run Means for Your Trip</h2>
    <p>The fall run puts big predators on the move around New Smyrna Beach and Daytona Beach. September and October are when oversized <a href="/redfish">redfish</a> show up and reds take over the backwaters, with <a href="/inshore#snook">snook</a> mixed in. See what we caught in our <a href="/fishing-reports/new-smyrna-beach-fishing-report-september-2026">September</a> and <a href="/fishing-reports/new-smyrna-beach-fishing-report-october-2026">October</a> reports.</p>
    <p>Want to see it for yourself? Book an <a href="/inshore">inshore trip</a> or call Capt. Chad at <a href="{{ site.phoneHref }}">{{ site.phone }}</a>.</p>

